//
// --- densities: audit round 3 (2026-09-01) — the D4d density pass ----------
// Batch 5 / D4d ruled KEEP D4C STRICT, FIX THE DATA. Under D4c a row with no
// density admits its BASIS family only, so a density-less row silently
// refuses EVERY volume line — the Pixel field test's "2 tbsp lemon juice"
// and "8 cups kale". R1 already guarantees no VOLUME-DEFAULT row is bare, so
// the stranded set is the 30 mass/count-default rows the FAO fallback
// audited and could not match. Those rejections are NOT relitigated: FAO
// v2.0 still has no tofu, tortilla, seaweed or mushroom row. What is new is
// a source FAO never was:
//   (a) the same FDC food under its OTHER record. usda_links.jsonl links
//       eight of these rows to an FDC record with no volume food_portion,
//       while a sibling record of the same food is already in the committed
//       reference WITH a portion-derived density. Cited as
//       fdc_density:<fdc_id> — the sibling's id, NEVER usda_fdc:<id>, which
//       is the macro prefill's mark (Ingredient.isUsdaPrefilled reads it).
//   (b) an FDC record for a food the no-analogue MACRO rule keeps link-less
//       but which is physically this food (vegan cheese, meatless nugget).
//   (c) a family bracket — the move already made for shiitake mushroom 0.30
//       and tender green 0.10 — or a printed label, as for crispy shallot.
// Every value is inside R2 (0.03-2.0). Coverage 277/307 -> 296/307.
//
// The 11 rows STILL density-less are now a decision, not an accident. Each
// was re-read against FDC after the FAO verdict, and each stays bare because
// no volume line reaches it, or because nothing honest pins it:
//   corn tortilla, flour tortilla, tostada shell, english muffin — the
//     linked FDC records carry no volume portion and neither does any
//     sibling; nobody measures a flatbread or a muffin by the cup. Their
//     piece/oz defaults say everything a recipe line needs.
//   nori, kombu — sold as dried sheets and strips and counted as such.
//     FDC's 'Seaweed, laver/kelp, raw' (0.3381) is the fresh wet weed, a
//     different food from the dried sheet, so it is not borrowable.
//   lime — the fruit, by the piece. Its two volume forms are already their
//     own rows with their own densities (lime juice 1.0229, and the zest is
//     spooned as a measure), so the fruit row needs none.
//   star anise — a whole hollow pod, mostly air; FDC's only anise record is
//     ground seed (171316, 0.4531), a different substance entirely.
//   seitan — FDC has no seitan record at all. The meatless-analogue rows
//     (breaded nugget 0.5495, frankfurter 0.5917) are formed or coated
//     products, a different geometry from a cup of torn seitan, and a
//     ~30% guess on a protein's macros is worse than a flagged line.
//   tofu bacon, shiitake bacon — prepared dishes (marinated tofu strips,
//     roasted shiitake), not products FDC or FAO carries. FDC's 'Bacon,
//     meatless' 0.6087 is the commercial formed strip, and 'Mushrooms,
//     shiitake, stir-fried' 0.3762 is a wet stir-fry: neither is the
//     crisped strip these rows mean. Both are piece-default and stay so.
